s season  too but also that you got to spend time  now and work with the other cast because  you were in a solo appearance last  season so  how was that compared to your experience  with season three  oh it was so fun um mainly i think the  thing that like really was the most fun  for me  was like  all of the improv work that we got to do  especially with eduardo he plays argyle  um all of the scenes that we did he like  completely improved a lot of his stuff  that ended up making the final cut um  and so we would all be playing off of  him and  i think there's like one line that ended  up being in the final cut too that um  is like you're being sarcastic and i go  yeah and that was never scripted that  just kind of happened because finn was  like  there was a long silence and then he was  like i'm gonna say something and then he  said something and i was like it was a  lot of like playing off of each other  which i never got to have in season  three  and even at the beginning of season four  when i'm talking with dustin  you know it was just me and gayton all  along and getting to do a scene with a  bunch of different people  straight from doing a scene with one  person multiple times  like it was definitely shocking and all  of the like fun extra improv that we got  to do was like so memorable  yeah and you mentioned gate and i want  to bring that up because is it a real  challenge to play this powerful love  susie has for dustin but you guys  actually haven't been in the scene  together yet you get this is as long as  relationship is that challenging to kind  of get into that  right right yeah i feel like all the  fans are just waiting for them to meet  in real life  and like you don't see them in real life  because you know they're supposed to  have met like in summer camp but i don't  think that they've seen each other since  then you know in my mind which is which  is wild um but i actually i grew up with  gay in and i grew up just knowing his  family  so  hon